    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0410" n="396" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg396"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">622.3531/2: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-14T12:00:00-05:00">March 14,
                            1942—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 7:37 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>198. The Argentine Government has made preliminary overtures looking to a barter
                    agreement which would involve supplying crude rubber from Ecuador in return for
                    authorizing exports of tires from Argentina. The Minister of Finance<anchor
                        n="65" xml:id="d422-f1"/> desires an expression of opinion as to the
                    attitude of the United States to such an arrangement. Actually Argentina and
                    other buyers are offering higher prices for Ecuadoran rubber than is being
                    offered in the United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d422-f1" n="65" xml:id="d422-f1-content">
